Licence and sources

1. Lexifina's own work

The history as commits, the commit messages, the tables, the tools and the documentation are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

To the extent possible under law, Lexifina has waived all copyright and related or neighbouring rights to this work.

This dedication covers only Lexifina's own work. It does not cover the texts and records listed in section 2, which
are reproduced from their publishers and stay under whatever terms their publishers give them.

2. Texts and records from their publishers

Under the Portuguese Copyright Code (Código do Direito de Autor e dos Direitos Conexos, artigo 8.º, n.º 1, read with
artigo 3.º, n.º 1, alínea c)), systematic or annotated compilations of the texts of conventions, laws, regulations and
administrative or judicial decisions of the State, and their official translations, are not protected. None of the
texts here has legal value: only the act as published in the official journal, or the decision as given by its court,
is authentic. Each record names the page it was read from (`source`, or `fonte` in parlamento/) and the sha256 of
what was read.

2.1 Diário da República (INCM)
    legislacao/, codigos/, constituicao/, serie-2/, reguladores/aviso-banco-portugal/, and the acórdãos and assentos
    published in the Diário da República in jurisprudencia/ (acordao*, assento, 2001 to 2004).

    Source: Diário da República, Imprensa Nacional-Casa da Moeda, S.A. (INCM), https://diariodarepublica.pt. The current
    and earlier texts of consolidated acts are INCM's consolidated text (Legislação Consolidada), reproduced without
    INCM's notes. The DR's legal notice (Avisos Legais, https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/geral/avisos-legais, read on
    2026-10-28) says:

        O serviço público de acesso universal e gratuito do Diário da República é regulado pelo Decreto-Lei n.º 83/2016,
        de 16 de dezembro, e pelo Despacho Normativo n.º 16/2022, de 30 de dezembro, que estabelecem que este serviço é
        assegurado pela Imprensa Nacional-Casa da Moeda, S. A. (INCM), nos termos previstos no Decreto-Lei n.º 235/2015,
        de 14 de outubro.
        [...]
        O acesso universal e gratuito compreende a possibilidade de impressão, arquivo, pesquisa e livre acesso ao
        conteúdo dos atos publicados nas 1.ª e 2.ª séries do Diário da República.
        [...]
        A produção do texto consolidado dos atos publicados, ainda que sem valor legal, de modo a facilitar a consulta e
        a sistematização do ordenamento jurídico;

    ("The public service of universal and free access to the Diário da República is governed by Decreto-Lei n.º 83/2016
    [...] Universal and free access includes the possibility of printing, archiving, searching and free access to the
    content of the acts published in the 1st and 2nd series of the Diário da República. [...] The production of the
    consolidated text of published acts, though without legal value, to make the legal order easier to consult and
    systematise.")

    The same notice forbids only attempts to alter or upload information, or any action that could harm the system,
    and states no other condition on reuse. The consolidated text is produced as part of that public service. Lei n.º
    26/2016, as amended by Lei n.º 68/2021 (which transposes Directive (EU) 2019/1024 on open data and the reuse of
    public sector information), bars the public bodies it covers from using the database maker's right to prevent the
    reuse of their documents.

2.2 Courts
    jurisprudencia/jstj, jsta, jtca, jtcn, jtrl, jtrp, jtrc, jtre, jtrg, jcon, cajp
        Source: Bases Jurídico-Documentais, Instituto de Gestão Financeira e Equipamentos da Justiça (IGFEJ),
        Ministério da Justiça, http://www.dgsi.pt. Texts as published, anonymised by the publisher.
    jurisprudencia/tc, tc-decisoes-sumarias
        Source: Tribunal Constitucional, https://www.tribunalconstitucional.pt. Texts as published, anonymised by the
        publisher. The Court's site policy (https://tribunalconstitucional.pt/PesquisaAcordao/SitePolicy, read on
        2026-11-18) asks that the source be named and that the case law be stated not to be authentic; both are
        stated here and on each record.
    jurisprudencia/tribunal-contas
        Source: Tribunal de Contas, https://tcjure.tcontas.pt. Summaries as published.
    jurisprudencia/caad-tributario
        Source: CAAD - Centro de Arbitragem Administrativa, https://caad.org.pt. Tax arbitration decisions as CAAD
        publishes them under Decreto-Lei n.º 10/2011, artigo 16.º, anonymised by the publisher.

2.3 Assembleia da República
    parlamento/
        Source: Assembleia da República, open data (https://www.parlamento.pt, Dados Abertos),
        the Diário da Assembleia da República and the Debates Parlamentares (https://debates.parlamento.pt), whose
        text is the publisher's own OCR. Petitioners' names are left out (personal data of private persons).

2.4 Regulators and regions
    reguladores/anacom
        Source: ANACOM - Autoridade Nacional de Comunicações, https://www.anacom.pt. Decisions as published.
    regioes/joram
        Source: Jornal Oficial da Região Autónoma da Madeira (JORAM), https://joram.madeira.gov.pt. Texts read from
        the official PDFs.

3. Questions

A publisher who wants something here changed or removed can open an issue at
https://github.com/lexifina/portugal-law/issues.
